  - created_at: "2026-10-10T07:51:11.216Z"
    author: codex-regex-investigator
    text: "Independent codex-regex-investigator: bounded read-only investigation of CodeQL finding 16 / inline4236838359 at d937568; reconstruct tokenizer resource boundary and expansion semantics, run focused probes only, and propose compatible bounded parsing. No implementation edits or delegation."
  - created_at: "2026-10-10T07:53:54.036Z"
    author: codex-regex-investigator
    text: "Independent evidence at source d937568: package.json exports shell-scan and attestation; auditPublishAttestation -> publishInvocationsIn -> publishInvocationsInShell -> tokenizeCommands reaches shell-scan.ts:377 on arbitrary SourceFile.text. Direct callers also include caseDepthChange, scalarAssignmentEvents, shellScalarsByLine and recursive substitutions/YAML/evaluators. Missing-close regex ${ plus 1000/2000/4000 at-signs took 1.3/5.0/22.8 ms; tokenizer echo double-quote plus 100/200/400 repeated ${ prefixes and equal at-sign suffix took 1.6/15.5/121.9 ms, supporting quadratic single-call and cubic repeated-suffix hypotheses. Recursion depth limit does not bound this per-input CPU cost."
  - created_at: "2026-10-10T07:53:54.696Z"
    author: codex-regex-investigator
    text: "Independent semantics/proposal: quoted scalar $X or ${X} and quoted star expansions are single operands; quoted $@, array [@], nested default containing array [@], and name-prefix @ expansion can yield several. Mixed unquoted expansion plus quoted suffix remains multiword. Regex also flags scalar defaults containing mail@example, scalar @Q transformations and array-length expansions: preserve these conservative classifications in the resource fix. Proposed right-to-left index prepass resets at-sign state at each closing brace, records whether the first later brace exists and has an at-sign before it; constant-time dollar lookups preserve the existing regex without suffix slices or repeated searches. Ephemeral randomized differential probe passed 9033 dollar offsets; 3007/30007/300007 character prepasses took 0.057/0.327/3.058 ms. Keep quoted loop traversal so nested substitutions remain visible. Separate observed risk: unquoted echo ${X:-$(npm publish)} is swallowed by shell-scan.ts:398-418 and audits clean beside an attested sibling; quoted equivalent discovers the hidden publish. Root should verify this separately."
  - created_at: "2026-10-10T07:53:55.540Z"
    author: codex-regex-investigator
    text: "Focused verification only: node --test test/shell-command-scan.test.ts passed 12/12 via pm test --run --only-last --progress; node --test test/publish-indirection.test.ts passed 32/32 via pm test --run --match test/publish-indirection.test.ts --progress. Inline node --input-type=module resource/semantic/equivalence probes and inert bash argument-count probes passed; no source test artifacts added. PM test-result tracking is disabled, so results are documented here without configuration changes. No full gates, implementation edits, delegation, GitHub writes, publication or push. Investigation complete; root verifies and integrates, item remains open."
  - created_at: "2026-10-10T07:54:16.930Z"
    author: codex-regex-investigator
    text: "Direct-caller correction: attestation.ts:336 is startsIfSiblingArm, not caseDepthChange. Complete production call sites: attestation.ts:336,458,476,489 and shell-scan.ts:468,480,495,1245,1834. PM history verified clean after release; this correction is documentation only."
  - created_at: "2026-10-10T07:55:23.526Z"
    author: codex-root-regex
    text: "Root accepts CodeQL16 performance finding and independently confirms caller-controlled shell text reaches overlapping quoted-expansion regex. Plan TDD: actual bounded child refusal of unterminated/repeated dollar-brace inputs, compatibility cases for scalar/positional/array words, then monotone delimiter caches preserving the existing first-closing-brace contract. The independent nested unquoted command-substitution observation is a separate attestation scope, not silently certified by this performance repair."
  - created_at: "2026-10-10T07:56:40.168Z"
    author: codex-root-regex
    text: "Original real tokenizer child exceeds unchanged 2s budget with unterminated quoted dollar-brace plus80000 at-signs and fails the assertion; scalar/list compatibility controls pass. Root replaces the overlapping regex with monotone next-close/next-at caches, preserving raw first-closing-brace semantics and positional/array refusal. Test typecheck and focused actual parser/publication controls pass. Independent candidate review precedes final source gate."
  - created_at: "2026-10-10T07:57:24.317Z"
    author: codex-regex-reviewer
    text: "Independent candidate-only review started: inspect quoted expansion cache equivalence, direct caller refusal behavior, malformed delimiters and surviving resource paths. Source and tests read-only; no broad gates."
  - created_at: "2026-10-10T07:59:13.509Z"
    author: codex-regex-reviewer
    text: "Independent candidate review found a concrete semantic regression at shell-scan.ts:384-391: absent closing brace uses text.length sentinel, so any later at-sign makes multipleWords true. echo quoted dollar-brace-at reproduces old undefined versus candidate true; later comment/word at-sign can contaminate an unterminated parameter too. Focused linked command node --test --test-name-pattern='quoted expansion scanning|quoted scalar and list' test/publish-indirection.test.ts: 1 pass, 1 failure; malformed-input assertion fails (not timeout). 5832 structured differential cases yield48 differences, all added multipleWords; scalar, positional, array, nested and escaped closed forms retain old classification. Direct publisher operand boundary attestation.ts:537/544 therefore refuses extra malformed paths rather than permitting a newly hidden publisher. Each next-delimiter search is monotone, so changed classification searches are linear; isolated repeated malformed inputs40k/80k/160k complete in23/16/84ms, indicative only. Fix must distinguish missing closing brace from a real close before comparing indices; no implementation edited."
  - created_at: "2026-10-10T07:59:48.222Z"
    author: codex-regex-reviewer
    text: "Scope note: live source changed during review to add parameterClose < text.length at line391. That later guard is outside the supplied immutable candidate; the reported48 structured differences and1 failed focused test describe the supplied candidate before that edit. No source/test edits by this reviewer. Random probe ran after the external edit and is not evidence for the supplied candidate. Review follows both cache-refresh and cache-reuse branches, real versus absent delimiters,  fast path and literal/escaped-dollar bypass. No newly relaxed publisher boundary or newly polynomial search identified in the supplied change. General shell fidelity, other parser resource paths, package-wide gates and later guard verification remain root-owned. Independence limitation: while isolating PM changes, a shared tracker diff accidentally displayed prior rationale; core differential finding was reconstructed from source and direct probes, not a prior receipt."
