  - created_at: "2026-10-10T08:27:56.897Z"
    author: codex-nested-reviewer
    text: "Independent source invariant: every potentially executed publisher must be enumerated with its own argument evidence; an attested sibling cannot attest a hidden publisher. Literal single-quoted and escaped substitutions must remain data. Arithmetic operands must contribute only nested executable substitutions. Direct callers at attestation.ts:336,458,476,489 and shell-scan.ts:1274,1863 consume the flat ShellCommand[]; nested execution scope is not represented."
  - created_at: "2026-10-10T08:27:57.799Z"
    author: codex-nested-reviewer
    text: "Confirmed surviving bypass (pre-existing, still present): with X unset and an attested sibling, echo ${X:-`printf %s \\`npm publish; printf 0\\``} executes an additional unattested publisher in real Bash -e, exits 0, and auditPublishAttestation returns zero failures. Equivalent echo $((1 + `printf %s \\`npm publish; printf 0\\``)), its double-quoted form, and parameter-wrapped arithmetic all reproduce. shell-scan.ts:244 closes backticks at the first escaped delimiter; nested enumeration retains printf but omits npm. Baseline and candidate both return zero failures. This is an in-scope surviving nested-form bypass, not a new regression."
  - created_at: "2026-10-10T08:27:58.663Z"
    author: codex-nested-reviewer
    text: "Confirmed candidate regression through direct callers: FLAG=--provenance; then on separate lines echo ${X:-$(unset FLAG)}; npm publish $FLAG. Real Bash -e exits 0 and invokes npm publish --provenance because command substitution cannot unset the parent binding. Candidate refuses the final invocation as unresolved; baseline accepts. Arithmetic echo $((1 + $(unset FLAG;printf 0))) reproduces the same baseline-pass/candidate-fail result. attestation.ts:476 applies unsetNames from all newly enumerated nested commands to the parent scope; shellScalarsByLine at shell-scan.ts:1863 likewise deletes the parent binding. Flat enumeration needs scope-aware consumption or equivalent protection."
  - created_at: "2026-10-10T08:27:59.363Z"
    author: codex-nested-reviewer
    text: "Independent verification: node --test test/publish-indirection.test.ts passed 41/41; linked node --test test/publish-indirection.test.ts test/shell-command-scan.test.ts passed 53/53. PM test --run --progress also executed the item existing linked focused commands; all six passed (includes pack-prepare and windows-proof-history). Focused real-Bash controls covered quoted/unquoted/single-quoted/escaped/backtick/nested parameter and arithmetic forms, plus attested nested publishers. In-memory baseline differential confirmed changed rejects and both findings. ShellCommand[] token keys/types, literal snapshots, outer-first order, function length 1, and optional depth behavior remain compatible; source adds optional arithmetic boolean, dist declaration is unchanged until root build. Depth >8 still returns [], so bounded enumeration is not complete beyond that inherited cap. Existing hostile suffix deadline test passed. PM test result tracking is disabled; outcomes are documented here. Source/test files remained read-only and unstaged; root owns final verification and disclosure."
